  "id": "DrugBank_DB01009 - MONDO_8383",
  "verbalization": "Ketoprofen is implicated in the pathogenesis of Rheumatoid Arthritis through a chain of indications that connect it to arthropathic conditions. The evidence suggests that Ketoprofen is associated with Arthropathy, which in turn is linked to Piroxicam and Tiaprofenic Acid, both of which are indicated for Rheumatoid Arthritis. This indicates a potential pathway where Ketoprofen may influence arthropathic processes, possibly through mechanisms that affect inflammation or joint pathology. The overlapping indications between Ketoprofen and other drugs used for Rheumatoid Arthritis suggest a possible shared mechanism of action or a role in the development of arthropathic conditions that progress to Rheumatoid Arthritis. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering arthropathic conditions as intermediate steps in the relationship between Ketoprofen and Rheumatoid Arthritis.",
